            "State Council Executive Meeting on 19 September 2012. Since 2013, "
            "the third day of the annual National Energy Conservation Awareness "
            "Week has been designated as National Low-Carbon Day, aimed at "
            "disseminating knowledge about climate change, publicising the "
            "concept and policies of low-carbon development, encouraging public "
            "participation, and advancing the task of controlling GHG emissions. "
            "The first National Low-Carbon Day fell on 17 June 2013. The Day is "
            "led by the NDRC and the MEE, who jointly issue an annual activity "
            "notice with multiple departments (co-issued with the National Energy "
